# 🚀 Why These Concepts Matter in React

Modern JavaScript is the foundation of React.

You will use these concepts frequently when building React applications:

```text
Variables & Constants
        ↓
let / const
        ↓
Functions
        ↓
Objects & Arrays
        ↓
Destructuring
        ↓
Array Methods
        ↓
Template Literals
        ↓
React Components
        ↓
Props & State
```

### React Example

```javascript
function UserCard({ name, age }) {
    return (
        <div>
            <h2>{name}</h2>
            <p>Age: {age}</p>
        </div>
    );
}
```

Here:

- `name` and `age` are variables.
- `{name}` and `{age}` display JavaScript values.
- Objects are commonly used for data.
- Functions are used to create components.
- JavaScript expressions are heavily used inside JSX.

